    "body": "Closes #112.\n\nImplements ADR-012: box-model shorthands now expand to longhands, and layout consumes the longhands. This is the change that makes `p { margin: 10px 20px }` render for the first time.\n\n## The bug this fixes\n\nBefore this PR:\n\n```css\np { margin: 10px 20px }\n```\n\nproduced one `Declaration` with the raw value `\"10px 20px\"`. `parse_px` rejected multi-value input, so layout saw `0`. The margin silently vanished.\n\nSame for `margin-top: 10px` written directly — `fill_sides` read only the shorthand name `margin`, so the longhand was ignored.\n\n## The fix\n\nTwo coordinated changes, in one commit:\n\n### Parse-time expansion (`src/renderer/css/stylesheet.cpp`)\n\n- `split_tokens`: whitespace tokenizer\n- `is_box_shorthand`: guards `margin`, `padding`, `border-width`\n- `expand_shorthand`: 1/2/3/4 tokens -> four longhand `Declaration`s, per CSS 2.1 section 8.1\n- `add_declaration` calls `expand_shorthand`\n\nThe `important` flag propagates to each longhand. >4 or 0 tokens skip the declaration (matches CSS error handling).\n\n**Property name table, not string concatenation.** The first build failed with `\"border-width-top\" == \"border-top-width\"` — because for `border-width`, the `-width` suffix goes *inside* the name, not after the side. The fix uses an explicit per-shorthand name table:\n\n| Shorthand | Longhands |\n|---|---|\n| `margin` | `margin-top`, `margin-right`, `margin-bottom`, `margin-left` |\n| `padding` | `padding-top`, `padding-right`, `padding-bottom`, `padding-left` |\n| `border-width` | `border-top-width`, `border-right-width`, `border-bottom-width`, `border-left-width` |\n\n### Longhand consumption (`src/renderer/layout/layout.cpp`)\n\n`fill_sides` now takes four `const char*` property names instead of one base name. The three call sites pass the full longhand set. The `border-top-width` shape is handled without special-casing inside `fill_sides`.\n\n## One commit, not two\n\nThe issue planned two commits: parse-time expansion, then longhand consumption. A parse-only commit breaks the layout tests, because `fill_sides` would read `margin` which no longer exists in computed style. The two halves ship together to keep CI green at every commit.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `./build/tests/honeybee_tests \"[css][stylesheet]\"` -> **37 cases, 128 assertions, all pass**\n- `./build/tests/honeybee_tests \"[layout]\"` -> **23 cases, 97 assertions, all pass**\n- `./build/tests/honeybee_tests` -> **143 cases, 605 assertions, all pass** (was 130/527 before this PR)\n- `layout: margin stacking matches ADR worked example` still passes — the exact y=10/y=46 check from ADR-011's ASCII diagram — proving single-value shorthands behave identically\n- `grep -rl \"lexbor/\" src/` still returns exactly `src/renderer/html/convert.cpp`\n\n## Test changes\n\n- **9 new parse tests** in `test_stylesheet.cpp`: every row of ADR-012's parse table plus the too-many-values and `important` cases\n- **4 new layout tests** in `test_layout.cpp`: margin 2-value, padding 4-value, border-width 2-value, margin-top longhand\n- **1 existing test updated**: `stylesheet: real-world example` previously expected `margin: 0 0 1em 0` to produce 1 declaration (raw shorthand); ADR-012 correctly produces 4 longhands, so the count is now 4\n\n## Deferred (per ADR-012)\n\n- `border` shorthand, `border-color` (requires `LayoutBox` struct change)\n- `background`, `font`, `overflow`, `list-style` shorthands\n- `calc()`, `var()`, CSS-wide keywords\n- `auto` margins\n- Named border widths (`thin`, `medium`, `thick`)\n\n## Next\n\nWith shorthand expansion landed, the next ADR candidates in order:\n\n1. **UA stylesheet** — `<h1>` at 2em, `<body>` margin 8px, `<em>` italic. High visible payoff on every page.\n2. **Inline formatting** — `<span>`, `<a>`, `<em>`, text wrapping. The biggest structural gap for real pages.\n\nEach its own ADR + issue + PR, same rhythm.\n",
